   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to the number of signatures for\nindependent nominating petitions; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S4380",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4380-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-142, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4380\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to the number of signa-\ntures for independent nominating petitions; and providing for the repeal\nof such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to amend the petition signature threshold for\nindependent nominating petitions in 2021.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 6-142 of the Election Law by reducing the mini-\nmum number of signatures required for independent nominating petitions.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRecently, the Legislature passed and the Governor signed Chapter 22 of\n2021 (5.2733 (May) / A.3356 (Bichotte-Hermelyn)), which lowered peti-\ntioning signature thresholds and adjusted the political calendar for\npetitioning in 2021 due to COVID-19. However, the aforementioned changes\nonly affect candidates registered in a political party. In order to\nensure safety during the COVID-19 pandemic, this bill would temporarily\nreduce the minimum number of signatures required for independent candi-\ndates by fifty percent.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNot yet determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately and shall\nexpire and be deemed repealed December 31, 2021.\n",
